xt Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5534203000">January 10, 2024</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">So I usually steer clear of ARCs, because I'm the type of reader who lives for spoilers. And ARCs are the ultimate unchartered, unspoiled territory. <em>Not my jam, ma'am!</em> But I jumped at the chance to listen to the the ARC audiobook for <em>Forbidden Warriors in Love</em>. Since I've already read &amp; loved these three novellas, there was zero risk - and the audiobook is <strong>duet </strong>narrated by J.F. Harding and Samantha Brentmoor... It was a no-brainer.<br /><br />This audiobook contains three standalone novellas set in the <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/series/306949-ruthless-warlords" rel="nofollow noopener">
  <i>Ruthless Warlords</i>
</a> universe:<br /><br />★ <a title="Forbidden Flame (Ruthless Warlords #1.5) by Alison Aimes" href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/56425857.Forbidden_Flame__Ruthless_Warlords__1_5_" rel="nofollow noopener">Forbidden Flame</a> (#6) <em>(formerly #1.5)</em><br />★ <a title="Princess Claimed (Ruthless Warlords) by Alison Aimes" href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/63110042.Princess_Claimed__Ruthless_Warlords_" rel="nofollow noopener">Princess Claimed</a> (#7)<br />★ <a title="War Prize of the Beast A Dark Fated-Mates Romance (Ruthless Warlords #8) by Alison Aimes" href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/123853106.War_Prize_of_the_Beast_A_Dark_Fated_Mates_Romance__Ruthless_Warlords__8_" rel="nofollow noopener">War Prize of the Beast</a> (#8) (originally appeared in the <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/61220895.Ruled_By_The_Alpha_A_Dystopian_Omegaverse_Anthology" title="Ruled By The Alpha A Dystopian Omegaverse Anthology by Nora Ash" rel="noopener">Ruled By The Alpha</a> anthology<br /><br /><strong>🎙 J.F. Harding</strong> is one of my favorite narrators. I've listened to him play a beast (<a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/61068458.The_Beast__Monsters_and_Beauties___1_" title="The Beast (Monsters and Beauties, #1) by Jenika Snow" rel="noopener">The Beast</a>), an alien (<a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/57900429.Mandy_and_the_Tentacle_Monster__Urf_Oomons___1_" title="Mandy and the Tentacle Monster (Urf Oomons, #1) by Bebe Harper" rel="noopener">Mandy and the Tentacle Monster</a>), and a self-made American industrialist (<a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/58029168.Crying_Wolfe__Goode_Girls___5_" title="Crying Wolfe (Goode Girls, #5) by Kerrigan Byrne" rel="noopener">Crying Wolfe</a>) - and he made them all feel authentic. In <em>Forbidden Flame</em> and <em>Princess Claimed</em>, he brings a slightly wicked, wry tone to his voice. And then he gets extra-growly in <em>War Prize.</em> 🥵<br /><br /><strong>🎙 Samantha Brentmoor</strong> also did a great job. This was my first time listening to her, and she reminded me a bit of Stella Hunter, but with a subtle hint of Kathleen Turner smokiness. (Not to go all "Ursula" here - but I wish I had her voice!)<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br />One thing I love about the <em>Ruthless Warlords</em> series is how it shakes up the power imbalances inherent in Omegaverse. Don't get me wrong - Anarcheim is in nothing like <em>Sweetverse</em>. But in this world, Omegas can have superpowers - and finding their fated mates dials up those powers. Which <em>means</em> their Alpha mates don't have all the control, and they're forced to step up their game and learn how to <em>compromise</em> and <em>communicate</em>. It's awesome and I find it oddly adorable too.<br /><br />All of these novellas are interconnected but fine standalone. (<em>War Prize</em> especially exists in it's own bubble.) That said, you'll get more context if you're already familiar with this universe. And since the first book is one of my top favorites <em>ever, </em> I'll always recommend starting there.<br /><br />For convenience, I'm posting my separate reviews for all three novellas below:<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br /><strong>(#6) Forbidden Flame</strong><br /><br />Prior to this novella, Magnus' (MMC) uncle killed his father, usurped the throne, and banished him to the <em>Mad Max</em>-ish dystopian wasteland known as the Forbidden Sector. Naturally, he's out for revenge.<br /><br />In his pursuit to regain his birthright, he intercepts a deadly "weapon" - his fated mate, Amora (FMC). Too bad she's a literal femme fatale - one touch causes spontaneous combustion 🔥! When she goes in heat, they have to get very creative without touching 😏. I really loved the way the haze of rut kept playing with their minds. <br /><br />Magnus is a reluctant hero leading a ragtag band of castoffs in a gritty environment, so we see a bit of the "he upgrades for her" trope. The FMC is touch-starved of course, and I wanted more on that. I also wanted to learn more about Amora in general. But I love how determined and confident he was to make it work with her.<br /> <br /><strong>notes</strong> <em><strong> | </strong>omegaverse<strong> | </strong>fated mates<strong> | </strong>insta<strong> | </strong>revenge pawn<strong> | </strong>both MCs reluctantly morally gray<strong> | </strong>virgin FMC<strong> | </strong>size kink<strong> | </strong>mutual masturbation<strong> | </strong>dirty talk<strong> | </strong></em><br /><br /><strong>⚠ CWs (partial):</strong> dark themes, graphic violence, physical/sexual threats (not by MCs), references to past abuse, and inherent Omegaverse power imbalances.<br /><br />⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4.25 stars)<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br /><strong>(#7) Princess Claimed</strong><br /><br />We first meet Pavel (MMC) in <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/56425857.Forbidden_Flame__Ruthless_Warlords__1_5_" title="Forbidden Flame (Ruthless Warlords #1.5) by Alison Aimes" rel="noopener">Forbidden Flame</a> - he's Magnus' loyal comrade with the broken horn. <br /><br />He craves solitude due to his PTSD - but then Ari (FMC) literally falls into his arms. She was on the run from baddies when she temporarily loses her sight &amp; memory. Her powers are Unlocking, and a mix of X-ray vision &amp; "radar sense". <br /><br />Personally, I'm not a fan of the Amnesia trope, but I really liked the rest. My heart ached for Pavel and what he endured. The FMC is kind of <em>(spoiler)</em> <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="dd2b586c-51b4-42c3-a626-12e44fa2a527" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="dd2b586c-51b4-42c3-a626-12e44fa2a527">like Robin Hood</label>, and I appreciate morally gray FMCs. There were also some creatively spicy scenes. And if you ever felt personally victimized by <em>Casablanca, </em>this felt like a fun, reimagined HEA.<br /><br />This is fine standalone, but you'll get a little more context if you read <em>Forbidden Flame</em> first.<br /><br /><strong>notes</strong> <em><strong> | </strong>omegaverse | fated mates<strong> | </strong>INSTA!<strong> | </strong>amnesia<strong> | </strong>both MCs morally gray<strong> | </strong>scarred hero<strong> | </strong>no virgins<strong> | </strong>size kink<strong> | </strong>praise kink<strong> | </strong>sex toys<strong> | </strong> </em><br /><br /><strong>⚠ CWs (partial):</strong> dark themes, graphic violence, physical/sexual threats (not by MCs), PTSD flashbacks including death &amp; claustrophobia, and inherent Omegaverse power imbalances.<br /><br /><em>(PS not sure if it's still around, but there was some very 🥵 fan art for this couple in a past newsletter.)</em><br /><br />⭐⭐⭐⭐ (3.75 stars)<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br /><strong>(#8) War Prize of the Beast</strong><br /><br />Take the chaotic mindset from one of Ruby Dixon's <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/33858773.Fire_in_His_Blood__Fireblood_Dragon___1_" title="Fire in His Blood (Fireblood Dragon, #1) by Ruby Dixon" rel="noopener">Fireblood Dragons</a>, and mix him with one of Lizzy Bequin's <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/55439802.Meat__Ukkur_Mates__1_" title="Meat (Ukkur Mates #1) by Lizzy Bequin" rel="noopener">Ukkur Mates</a> - and you've got Cheim! <br /><br />Somewhere on a distant, primitive planet, he's lost in a red haze of instinct and violence - and plans to eat Anara (FMC). Then he scents her, and decides to <em>eat</em> her instead 😏. Unfortunately for him, that's when she discovers her power of Levitation. This story was kinda bonkers - and I loved it even more on my second read. The first time I missed some of the cuteness because I was like 🫣 <em>"How dark is this going to get?"</em> (I first read it in the <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/61220895.Ruled_By_The_Alpha_A_Dystopian_Omegaverse_Anthology" title="Ruled By The Alpha A Dystopian Omegaverse Anthology by Nora Ash" rel="noopener">Ruled By The Alpha</a> anthology.)<br /><br />Our MMC discovers these fuzzy new <em>feelings</em> - and it's adorable. He decides all he wants is to keep hearing her happy purrs - and is determined to figure out how. I thought it was cute AF! <br /><br />BIG spoiler (I didn't see it coming, at least!): <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="80e044f5-42b4-4a17-9a94-76e5a430e86a" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="80e044f5-42b4-4a17-9a94-76e5a430e86a">Turns out this is a prequel for the entire series. Set in the distant past, it acts as an origin story for the <em>Anar-Cheim</em> universe. That was brilliant - but a slight bummer for me, because their descendants eventually exist in Anarcheim's dystopia. No worries, the couple definitely gets an HEA - but I've been told, on occasion, that <em>perhaps</em> I tend to overthink things... 🥴</label><br /><br /><br /><strong>notes<em> |</em></strong><em> omegaverse<strong> | </strong>fated mates<strong> | </strong>insta<strong> | </strong>primitive MCs<strong> | </strong>virgin MMC<strong> | </strong>size kink<strong> | </strong>"do I eat her or do I </em>eat <em>her?"</em>😏<em>
  <strong> |</strong>
</em><br /><br /><strong>⚠ CWs (partial):</strong> dark themes, graphic violence, gore, initial dubcon, and inherent Omegaverse power imbalances.<br /><br /><em>(PS there is some extremely 🥵 fan art for this couple if you get the author's newsletter!)</em><br /><br />⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4.75 stars)<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br />The <em>
