age and to NOT open the bag. But when it begins to move, his curiosity gets the better of him and he opens it. He never expected to come face to face with her or to have his baser instincts kick in. Before she can escape, Amora is unpacked and finds herself being claimed by a large, ferocious alpha. <br /><i> Princess Claimed </i>– A princess is on the run with no memory of who she is and in need of help. He is a exile alpha who learned it’s much safer to help himself and himself only. That is, until his fated mate falls into his arms, quite literally. Now, he will do anything to possess and protect what’s his. <br /><i> War Prize of the Beast </i> – One is soft, little, and prey while the other is the apex predator, big, and fierce. One is designed to conquer, kill, and to be an alpha. The other, to run, hide, and be killed. When the most feared creature captures its prize, he is expecting his usual conquest, but what he gets is the furthest from the truth. <br /><br />This box set is narrated by the fantastic duo Samantha Brentmoor and J.F. Harding. These two narrators need more narrations together. Samantha brought such life, strength, and a side of vulnerability to all three of the omegas in these inter-galactic stories. J.F. Harding as these three ferocious alpha males is the dark to Brentmoor’s light. He is everything you want in a alpha-hole mate, he is deep and growly and yet he is charming and one hundred percent swoon-worthy. Again, these two narrators need more audiobooks together.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/19986299?shelf=books-of-2023" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">books-of-2023</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__contain